From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a container query unknown at first still depends on
 its units

ContainerQueryEvaluator caches a query's result unless its units say it
can change without the evaluator hearing of it: rem, viewport and
container units. MediaQueryEvaluator::EvalFeature recorded a feature's
units only after evaluating it, so a width query evaluated while its
container had no size came back unknown with no units. The cache kept
that result through a root font size change, and with expensive
DCHECKs on, the next evaluation failed
`result.unit_flags == actual.unit_flags (0 vs. 2)` in
container_query_evaluator.cc. Manganese's title bar hides itself with
`@container (max-width: 10rem)`, which hit it now and then in the VM
tests and guard-shell-manganese.

EvalFeature now records the units before it can return unknown.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
---
 third_party/blink/renderer/core/css/media_query_evaluator.cc | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/css/media_query_evaluator.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/css/media_query_evaluator.cc
index 16f9d12f97722..531aa476fe76b 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/css/media_query_evaluator.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/css/media_query_evaluator.cc
@@ -1646,6 +1646,14 @@ KleeneValue MediaQueryEvaluator::EvalFeature(
     NOTREACHED();
   }
 
+  // A feature's units are a dependency whether or not it can be evaluated
+  // yet: a container query that was unknown while its container had no size
+  // must still be dropped from ContainerQueryEvaluator's cache when the root
+  // font size or the viewport changes.
+  if (result_flags) {
+    result_flags->unit_flags |= feature.GetUnitFlags();
+  }
+
   if (!media_values_->Width().has_value() && feature.IsWidthDependent()) {
     return KleeneValue::kUnknown;
   }
@@ -1710,7 +1718,6 @@ KleeneValue MediaQueryEvaluator::EvalFeature(
         result_flags->is_viewport_dependent || feature.IsViewportDependent();
     result_flags->is_device_dependent =
         result_flags->is_device_dependent || feature.IsDeviceDependent();
-    result_flags->unit_flags |= feature.GetUnitFlags();
   }
 
   return result ? KleeneValue::kTrue : KleeneValue::kFalse;
